Subj: Real names only (and why)
Date: 07-04-88 11:05

A few people have asked why I dropped handles when we reopened.

When the board was The Pit, it was twenty of us who all knew each
other.  Now we get callers from Atlanta and California and, for some
reason, a very persistent gentleman in Springfield, Illinois.  A real
name makes a message board feel like a room full of people instead of a
room full of masks.  People are kinder with their names on.

Exceptions: none.  The Byte Bandit says "The Byte Bandit" IS his real
name.  He is on probation until he produces a birth certificate.

The old handles live on the Wall of Fame (bulletin 7), with honours.

-- Europa
