Subj: ARM-DOS 4.00 is running the board
Date: 06-02-89 23:50

The ARM Pit now runs ARM-DOS 4.00.  The upgrade took twenty minutes, or
two hours if you count the time I spent playing with DOSSHELL.

The one thing you will notice: ZMODEM.  It checks every block, resends
what the line noise ate, and picks up where it left off if the call
drops.  Use it.  Bulletin 3 tells you how.

The one thing you will not notice: MEM says the board leaves 540K of my
640K free.  I'm told this is excellent.  I'm keeping the other 100K for
emergencies.

-- Europa
