From: Europa Sysop
To: All
Subj: Happy 1990 (the clock was right)
Date: 01-01-90 00:01

Happy New Year from the spare bedroom!

I dialed the time service in Boulder at 11:50 last night, set the board
clock, and watched it roll over from 12-31-89 23:59:59 to 01-01-90
00:00:00 at exactly the moment the neighbours started banging pots.  I
may have cheered louder than the neighbours.

By tomorrow it will be two seconds slow again.  The ARM/AT is a
wonderful computer with the timekeeping instincts of a sundial.  I will
keep fighting.

Here's to a new decade of bad line noise and good company.

-- Europa
