Date: 04-01-90 00:05

Big news, everyone.  As of tonight The ARM Pit is connected to the phone
company's new DIGITAL LINE.  Callers with the right modem will connect
at 56,000 bits per second.  That is twenty-three times faster than
2400.  A 40K file in under ten seconds.  The whole message base before
your coffee cools.

How does it work?  The line is digital on my end and analog on yours,
and the modem does clever things with the difference.  I'd explain
more, but the explanation is at the phone company, and the phone
company is closed today.

The welcome screen has been updated to say so.

-- Europa

P.S. Please check today's date before you call your modem manufacturer.
