    there.  Try the one called WOPR.  It won't answer.  Probably.

-- Europa
@@14
From: Europa Sysop
To: All
Subj: New in the file area: a disk optimizer!
Date: 10-06-90 21:45

New in file area 1 (ARM-DOS Utilities): DEFRAG11.ZIP, the ARM Disk
Optimizer, version 1.1.  Inside: DEFRAG.EXE, DEFRAG.DOC (read it!) and
the FILE_ID.DIZ description.

Why you want it: when DOS saves a file, it puts the pieces wherever it
finds free room.  Delete a few files, save a few more, and after a year
your spreadsheet lives in fourteen places across the disk.  Every time
you load it, the heads have to go and fetch all fourteen.  That's
fragmentation, and that's why your two-year-old hard disk sounds busier
and feels slower than it did on the first day.

A disk optimizer picks all the pieces up and puts each file back
together, in one run, in order.  The heads stop wandering.  The disk
gets quieter.  Things load faster.  It is deeply satisfying to watch.

How to get it:

  1. F at the Main Menu, A to change to area 1.
  2. D, then DEFRAG11.ZIP, then Z for ZMODEM.
  3. On your machine:   UNZIP DEFRAG11.ZIP
  4. Read DEFRAG.DOC before you run anything.

And please, BACK UP FIRST.  A defragmenter moves every file you own.  It
is careful, and your power is probably reliable, and the 2:10 freight
probably won't shake anything loose.  I have said "probably" before.
Ask me about leap day.

I ran it on the board's disk last night.  CHKDSK is happy, the message
base loads faster, and Parity slept through the whole thing on top of
the modem.

-- Europa
